[ti:Solitude as Weapon]
[ar:EdgarAllanMusic]
[al:EcceH.text (Revalued)]
[00:16.84]I built my nest on the highest tree
[00:20.98]The one they call the Future
[00:23.45]The eagles bring what's good for me
[00:27.53]And nothing unclean gets through here
[00:29.93]The wind cuts like an honest word
[00:33.18]The cold burns bright and keeps me young
[00:36.35]I stacked the silence stone by stone
[00:39.75]Until the view was mine alone
[00:43.77]The hunger taught me how to taste
[00:48.42]Now I devour life and leave no trace
[00:54.01]This air that burns
[00:57.91]Is the cleanest thing I own
[01:06.54]Solitude's a weapon
[01:10.96]You can only hold alone
[01:20.33]I walk old roads with lighter feet
[01:23.52]The best thoughts find me out of doors
[01:26.73]The ice is close, the sun is sweet
[01:30.01]And down below the valley snores
[01:33.17]It isn't hate, it's just the air
[01:36.52]I simply can't breathe what they share
[01:39.73]A sense of cleanliness, that's all
[01:42.83]I smell a lie from way up there
[01:48.68]The hunger taught me how to taste
[01:53.25]Now I devour life and leave no trace
[01:59.09]This air that burns
[02:02.84]Keeps the borrowed voices low
[02:11.49]Solitude's a weapon
[02:15.87]Only clean hands get to hold
[02:24.08]It isn't steel, it doesn't strike
[02:27.18]It's a door I choose to close
[02:30.60]I guard myself with distance
[02:33.33]I heal myself by breathing slow
[02:37.87]Naked and free, I'll meet the day
[02:41.06]And laugh the way the morning does
[02:47.66]Not hiding. Breathing
[02:50.81]This air that burns
[02:54.74]Is the cleanest thing I own
[03:03.42]One must be made for it
[03:07.77]I was made for it alone
[03:11.51]
